#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A stand-in for `claude -p` and `codex exec` in the AI panel flows, so they never spend anyone's subscription.

It takes the same arguments, refuses to run unless Nuzky passed every flag that keeps the agent to
Nuzky's tools, and answers in Claude Code's stream-json or Codex's JSON lines. It is a real MCP client
of the bridge from --mcp-config or -c, so its edits go through Nuzky like a real agent's. Claude reads
stream-json user messages from stdin while it works; Codex reads one prompt up to EOF. The message picks what it does:
  "cut"      reads the project and its activity, says a message before and after opening its run, cuts 1-3 s out,
             adds two captions and answers
  "retakes"  transcribes, retries a declined model three times, or cuts the first two words in one run
  "options"  offers two takes with suggest_options
  "numbered list"  answers with loose Markdown lists: numbered from 1, numbered on from 4, and bullets
  "work as reels"  (Find reels) proposes four reels of at least 15 s from the transcript
  "slow"     opens a run, splits the clip and keeps working until stopped
  "steer me" splits at 2 s, waits for another message and splits at 4 s if it says "split", in the same run;
             Codex keeps working until stopped, like "slow"
  "long job" starts an export (into LOG/folder when the message says "folder") and ends its turn asking whether to wait; "Wait and continue" then reads that job
             (from $NUZKY_FAKE_AGENT_LOG/job.json) until it ends, "Stop the export" cancels it first
  "transcribe" transcribes with the small model and waits on the job until it ends; "transcribe again" recognises
             the files anew
  "keep: …"  sent from Your style: reads the style and keeps the rest of the message as the creator's rule
  the `thumbnail` prompt (Make a thumbnail): sets both covers in one run with the hook from "Hook: …" in the wishes,
             looks at the cover with inspect_thumbnail, waiting for its mask, and exports nothing
  "think first"  (Codex) says nothing for 2 s, then is echoed back
  "image gen" (Codex) makes the 9:16 cover from a generated orange PNG: looks at a frame, imports the PNG and sets the
             cover's image with the hook GROKBOT in front, as the guide's cover from a generated picture says
  "image"    (Codex) generates an orange PNG into a Codex home of its own (generated_images/<thread>/) as Codex's image_gen does, imports it with
             import_media and shows it as a picture in picture from 0, as Nuzky's instructions ask
  "signin"   is not signed in;  "limit" has hit its usage limit
  a message with pictures or a video attached says how many it got, with the size of each picture
  anything else is echoed back.
Each start is logged to $NUZKY_FAKE_AGENT_LOG/runs.jsonl (argv, pid, session, the pictures' sizes), and each message
Claude got while working to steered.jsonl; sessions live there too.
With $NUZKY_FAKE_AGENT_LOG/vanish, `--version` takes this executable's execute bit away, so the turn cannot start.
`auth status` (Claude) and `login status` (Codex) answer as the real ones, signed out with FAKE_AGENT_SIGNED_OUT=1.
With FAKE_AGENT_OLD=1, Claude is a version that does not know `--no-session-persistence`, so it names no models.
`mcp get nuzky` reads the agent's own settings: Codex prints the entry as JSON, Claude really starts the server and
reports whether it answered; with FAKE_AGENT_MCP=broken it starts it in an empty runtime folder, so it finds no app.
"""
